<title>GERMANY: Schmidhuber - EMU council plan not backed by Treaty.</title>
<headline>Schmidhuber - EMU council plan not backed by Treaty.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank board member Peter Schmidhuber said on Friday France's proposal for an economic council to act as a counterpart to an independent European Central Bank was given no support in the Maastricht Treaty.</p>
<p>&quot;Such an idea does certainly not find any support within the EC Treaty,&quot; he said in a speech to a forum on European and Monetary Union.</p>
<p>France has proposed that an informal gathering of ministers of those countries which take part in EMU take place to coordinate policy issues. The Bundesbank argues that this could impinge on the neutrality of the European Central Bank.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
